<title>SOUTH KOREA: West breaks ground for nuclear plants in N.Korea.</title>
<headline>West breaks ground for nuclear plants in N.Korea.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Representatives of nine countries and the European Union on Tuesday broke ground for a landmark nuclear project in communist North Korea, Seoul officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The international community is due to build two, 1,000-megawatt light-water reactors in the communist state in return for Pyongyang's promise to freeze and eventually dismantle its suspected atomic weapons programme.</p>
</text>
